<title>USA: Petroleum Heat cuts div, extends notes.</title>
<headline>Petroleum Heat cuts div, extends notes.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroleum Heat and Power Co Inc said on Wednesday it would cut its annual dividend to $0.30 per share from $0.60 per share, as part of its strategy to de-leverage its capital structure.</p>
<p>The company also said it reached an agreement in principle to extend the final maturity on $60 million of its institutionally held senior and subordinated notes from 1998 to 2002.</p>
<p>In conjunction with the extension, $30 million of those notes would be converted from subordinated to senior debt, Petroleum Heat said.</p>
</text>
